    ('h2', 'The honest audit: what v1 did not contain'),
    ('p', 'An honest answer to "are we sure this is the best we got" starts by admitting what was not there. The v1 blueprint was strong exactly where blueprints are supposed to be strong: the monolith decision, the provider-blind pipeline, the routing policy with enumerated escalation triggers, the cost model, and the model catalog were all specified to a level that survived review. But a blueprint deliberately stays above the implementation waterline, and sixteen things that a real build needs were left above that line with it. Each of them, left open, would have cost an unplanned decision in the middle of a coding session - which is exactly the kind of decision that gets made badly. The register below lists all sixteen, why each one matters, and the chapter of this dossier that closes it.'),
